Echo Dot 3 (MT7668, Amazon's wlan_mt76x8_sdio): advertise one PTKSA replay counter.

wpa_supplicant 2.11 advertises 16 PTKSA replay counters in its RSNE whenever the
association uses HT/VHT or the AP carries WMM (wpa_supplicant.c, "Mark WMM
enabled"). Amazon's driver writes its own RSNE into the association request
with RSN Capabilities 0, so the AP sees 0x0000 there and 0x000c in EAPOL-Key
msg 2/4, and drops the station after msg 2/4 (reason 2) as for a wrong key.
2.10 and Fire OS's 2.6 send 0x0000 in both and join. Bench-tested 2026-10-23.

--- a/src/rsn_supp/wpa_ie.c
+++ b/src/rsn_supp/wpa_ie.c
@@ -110,10 +110,6 @@
 {
 	u16 capab = 0;

-	if (sm->wmm_enabled) {
-		/* Advertise 16 PTKSA replay counters when using WMM */
-		capab |= RSN_NUM_REPLAY_COUNTERS_16 << 2;
-	}
 	if (sm->mfp)
 		capab |= WPA_CAPABILITY_MFPC;
 	if (sm->mfp == 2)
